**Summary of Vulnerabilities:**

All identified vulnerabilities are **Critical** and fall under the category of **Resource Leak (Iterator Not Closed)**. The core issue is the consistent failure to call the `Close()` method on iterators returned by state query functions (`GetStateByRange`, `GetStateByPartialCompositeKey`). This oversight leads to unreleased resources (gRPC streams, database cursors) on the peer nodes, which can cause severe performance degradation and eventual system instability due to resource exhaustion.

**No other vulnerability types (access control, input validation, read-after-write, private data leakage, non-deterministic operations, insecure key management) were detected in this specific code snippet.**
